AB  - The article discusses how professional indemnity insurers are increasingly focused on the risks associated with the use of artificial intelligence by firms, emphasising concerns such as the use of AI without adequate human checks and the handling of confidential data. It outlines what insurers want to know about AI use, including governance, oversight, training and risk management practices that can influence liability and underwriting decisions. 
KW  - Artificial intelligence; Insurance risk; Insurers; Underwriting; Risk management; Confidential data; AI governance
